package trion edition "0.2.0-draft.1"

include "sentences.trion"
include "words.trion"
include "composition.trion"
include "catalog.trion"
include "verification.trion"
include "evidence.trion"
include "proof.trion"
include "documents.trion"
include "tool.trion"
include "limits.trion"
include "propositional/analysis.trion"

namespace trion:
    use formal
    use software

    primitive person, problem, readability, rigor, system, source

    system trion processor, trion command, trioc command, language server, trion language, language rule, metatheoretic proof, proof obligation, specification consistency proof obligation, citation, section, missing case that trion processor report, trusted base member
    environment person, external proof checker

    section "What trion is":
        The trion language means a formal specification language that is a controlled natural language.
        A statement means a sentence of the trion language.
        A specification means a set of statements.
        An author means a person or a program that writes a specification.
        A reader means a person who reads a specification.

        Each statement has exactly one formal meaning.
        The trion language has a strict syntax and a formal semantics.
        The trion processor means the program that reads a specification and converts that specification.
        The theory of contracts means the theory of assume-guarantee contracts.

        A specification has consistency, compatibility, correctness, and completeness.

        [TRION-COMPILER]
        The trion processor shall convert each specification into the proof obligations of the consistency, the compatibility, the correctness, and the completeness of the specification.

        [TRION-THEORY]
        The trion processor shall follow the theory of contracts.

    section "A specification is a document":
        Each specification describes a system.
        Each specification is a document.
        The documentation of a system means a document that a reader reads in order to understand the system.

        [TRION-DOCUMENT]
        Each specification shall serve as the documentation of a system.

        [TRION-RIGOR-FIRST]
        If readability conflicts with rigor, then the trion language shall prefer rigor.

    section "A specification rests on evidence":
        Evidence means a source that states the origin or the rationale of a statement.
        An origin means a source that yields a statement.
        A rationale means a problem that a statement solves.
        The validity of a specification means the fitness of the specification for the problem of an author.

        [TRION-EVIDENCE]
        Each statement shall have evidence.

        [TRION-EVIDENCE-AUDIT]
        The trion processor shall trace each statement to the evidence of the statement.

        Verification guarantees the internal consistency of a specification.
        Evidence guarantees no validity.
        A person audits the validity of a specification with the evidence of the specification.
